   "he": "וְהָעֵדִים חוֹתְמִין עַל הַגֵּט מִפְּנֵי תִּיקּוּן הָעוֹלָם: מִפְּנֵי תִּיקּוּן הָעוֹלָם?! דְּאוֹרָיְיתָא הוּא, דִּכְתִיב: ״וְכָתוֹב בַּסֵּפֶר וְחָתוֹם״!",
   "en": "§ The mishna taught: «And the witnesses sign the bill of divorce for the betterment of the world.» The Gemara asks: Is the reason that the witnesses sign the bill of divorce «for the betterment of the world? It is by Torah law» that they must sign, «as it is written: “And subscribe the deeds, and sign» them, and call witnesses” (Jeremiah 32:44)."
